      "gap": "Source chronology and separating boundaries not fully preserved: (a) Milton p.3-4 states that the Topics A12 passage (105a12-19) is the earliest of Aristotle's three discussions of epagoge; the body (lines 194-206) gives the Topics characterization without the A12/105a12-19 locator or its chronological position as earliest. (b) Milton p.29 states that there is no further discussion of induction in the works Descartes published; the body (lines 1168, 1247-1252) says only that induction plays no significant role in the mature philosophy, which is a different claim. (c) Milton p.8 presents Alcinous's two-sentence treatment as indicating the lack of any serious interest in induction among the Platonists; the body (lines 404-413) reports the brevity but not Milton's inference from it. Reconstruct each of these with Milton's qualification at the cited pages.",
